The discrete-log connection has direct prior art: Harvey traces \(a^{p+q}=a^{N+1}\pmod N\) to Pollard’s 1978 kangaroo paper and McKee–Pinch’s 1996 algorithm. One caveat for experiments: an interval discrete log may have several solutions. Recovering a matching exponent does not by itself prove it is \(p+q\); candidates need validation or an order argument.

